Description: A unified set of functions to visualize sports data across the
    National Football League, National Basketball Association, Women's
    National Basketball Association, Major League Baseball, National Hockey
    League, and college football and basketball in 'ggplot2' plots, 'gt'
    tables and 'reactable' tables. Team logos, wordmarks and player headshots
    can be drawn as geoms, as axis text and inside table cells, and team color
    scales map team identifiers to their official colors. Team abbreviations
    used by different data providers, including historical abbreviations of
    relocated franchises, are cleaned to one canonical key per sport. Built on
    'ggpath' following the conventions of 'nflplotR' and designed to work with
    the companion 'SportsDataverse' data packages.
